# {{id}}

A Maktaba plugin made with `mkp new js` (Epic 54). It runs in maktaba-plugind's sandbox: no
network, no files, only the plugin API calls its manifest asks for and the admin grants.

```sh
npm install -g @bytecodealliance/jco @bytecodealliance/componentize-js
mkp build .                                    # plugin.js to package/plugin.wasm, then the home's checks
mkp test package --stage hello                 # run it in the harness
mkp pack package {{id}}.mkplugin               # the file to install (Settings, Plugins)
```

- **No WASI.** The build turns off every feature that would import WASI (`jco componentize
  --disable all`): no `fetch`, no `console` output, no clocks or random from WASI. Log with
  `write` from `maktaba:plugin/log`.
- **The world follows the manifest.** `mkp build` (or `mkp world .`) writes `wit/` so the
  plugin imports only the interfaces its capabilities cover; add a capability to
  `package/manifest.toml`, then build again to import its interface.
- TypeScript: compile to one ES module first (`tsc`, `esbuild`), and point the build at it
  with `mkp build . --entry dist/plugin.js`. `jco guest-types wit -o types` writes the types.

`mkp test --fixtures api.json` answers the plugin API from a file:
`{"library/video": {"id": "v1", "title": "A film"}}` (each key is `interface/function`).
